HOW TO COMPILE AND RUN
To compile:
    run the make command in terminal where the project is located.
To run the server:
    ./tsamgroup42 [port]
    where port is the port you want to run on
To run the client:
    ./client [ip-address] [port]
    where the ip and port is the ip-address and port of where the server is running

additional info:
    All code was compiled on linux, both on the TSAM server and locally on 
    Ubuntu through WSL.
    The server was run on the TSAM server at port 4042, which is hardcoded 
    in the server implementation

CLIENT-SERVER COMMUNICATION
commands:
    LISTSERVERS
        Lists all other servers our server is connected to
    GETMSG,GROUP_ID
        Gets one message that the server is storing for GROUP_ID. The 
        server then deletes that message. We intent for this to only be 
        getting messages that are for our group.
    SENDMSG,GROUP_ID,<message contents>
        Sends a message from our group to GROUP_ID. If the server know that 
        server, it sends the 
    CONNECT,GROUP_ID,<ip_address>,<port>
        Directly connect to a server at the ip_address and port

