KNOWN ISSUES
- segmentation faults
    - Sometimes when we accept a new connection, we get a segmentation 
    fault.
    - When we send a message from the client, the server might crash.
- The ports we list in our Clients vector is are not always correct, we try 
    are updating them to the correct value when we recieve SERVERS, but it 
    doesn't seem to be working all the time
- if another server is not following the protocol as specified on piazza
    (https://piazza.com/class/m02biihmqvn2up/post/277), our server will 
    most likely crash.
- cannot handle messages that do not fit in a TCP packet, or are longer
    than 5000 bytes
